        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): strip internal tool-trace banners from outbound text",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMicrosoft Teams outbound adapter did not strip internal tool-trace banners\nfrom assistant-visible text before delivery. Users could see internal\nscaffolding like `⚠️ 🛠️ search repos (agent) failed` in Teams messages.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded `sanitizeAssistantVisibleText` (the canonical shared sanitizer) to\n`msteamsChannelOutbound` via the `sanitizeText` hook. This matches the fix\nalready applied to tlon (#103450) and synology-chat (#102925).\n\nThe `msteamsOutbound` in `outbound.ts` is a runtime delegate (exposes\nsendText/sendMedia/sendPayload) — it does not need `sanitizeText` because\nthe delivery pipeline invokes the hook on `msteamsChannelOutbound`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** internal tool-trace banners visible in Teams messages\n**After:** internal scaffolding stripped, only user-visible prose delivered\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/msteams-sanitize-outbound` | Base: `upstream/main`\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nThe plugin-level tests assert against `msteamsPlugin.outbound.sanitizeText`\nwhich routes to `msteamsChannelOutbound` — the exact production adapter the\ndelivery pipeline invokes. The test verifies:\n- Tool-trace banners are stripped (\"Done.\\n⚠️ 🛠️ `search repos (agent)` failed\" → \"Done.\")\n- Normal prose passes through unchanged\n- Trace-only replies become empty strings\n\n### Regression tests\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/msteams/src/channel.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ msteamsPlugin > advertises sanitizeText that strips internal tool-trace banners from outbound text\n ✓ msteamsPlugin > sanitizeText returns empty string for trace-only replies\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  18 passed (18)\n```\n\n### Diff summary\n\n```\nextensions/msteams/src/channel.ts       | 4 ++ (import + sanitizeText hook)\nextensions/msteams/src/channel.test.ts  | 12 ++ (2 regression tests)\n```\n\nWhat was not tested: live Microsoft Teams transport (requires a registered\nTeams bot with Azure Bot Framework). The test exercises the exact production\ncallback that the delivery pipeline invokes — the same proof pattern accepted\nfor tlon (#103450) and synology-chat (#102925).\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
        "branch": "fix/msteams-sanitize-outbound",
